# ===========================================================================
# .gitignore — "never commit these files to git"
# ===========================================================================
# 🎯 WHAT THIS FILE DOES (plain English):
#   Tells git which local files to IGNORE. Things here are either huge
#   (node_modules, dist), full of secrets (.env), or temporary (*.log).
#   This keeps your repo small AND keeps passwords out of GitHub.
# ===========================================================================
node_modules/   # installed dependencies — reinstall any time with `npm ci`
dist/           # built frontend files — regenerated by `npm run build`
.env            # ⚠️ SECRETS — DB passwords etc. NEVER commit this!
*.log           # log files

.DS_Store       # macOS Finder junk
*.pem           # ⚠️ private SSH/SSL keys — never commit these!